{
  "_comment": "Lab Doctor demo catalog. Each lab = a Cosmos-authored spec (steps + validation definitions = expected ground truth) PLUS fleet telemetry as COHORTS. A cohort is a group of learners who exhibited the same outcome pattern; 'count' = how many learners it represents, so a handful of cohorts model a realistic fleet honestly and inspectably. 'history' = trailing daily health scores (illustrative trend for the sparkline). The catalog exercises every classifier: region DRIFT (A, D — same root cause => a cross-lab FLEET PATTERN), false-FAIL validation bug (A), false-PASS validation bug (F — the silent one), guide clarity (A, G), env/permission + quota (E), transient flake correctly downgraded (C), and healthy labs (B, H, I, J). Values illustrative; shapes mirror documented CloudLabs/Cosmos endpoints (see docs/architecture.md).",
